      "brief": "## Vercel AI Gateway Billing Dispute — Summary\n\n**Incident & Analysis** (Jul 8, 2026)\n\nA $183.24 charge appeared on the [REDACTED EMAIL] Vercel account via 9 \"AI Gateway Credits\" invoices. Initial investigation ruled out:\n- Active Stella backend usage of Vercel AI Gateway (confirmed not in use)\n- Leaked API key (would trip $25 auto-reload, not $20 manual purchases)\n- Account compromise (required login, not API access)\n\n**Root Cause Determination**\n\nPattern analysis identified a **billing bug**: seven identical $20 charges fired within a 28-second window (21:50:11–21:50:39 UTC), followed by two $21.62 charges ~17 minutes later — all clustered in an 18-minute burst around 2:50 PM UTC. This signature is consistent with an automated retry loop or webhook firing repeatedly, not human or API-driven spending.\n\n**Dispute Resolution** (Jul 8, 2026, ~6:09 PM)\n\nStella filed a support dispute with Vercel through the account-linked channel ([REDACTED EMAIL]), citing exact invoice timestamps and charge counts ($180 in erroneous duplicate credits) as evidence. The request demanded reversal of the duplicate charges as billing errors.\n\n**Status**: Dispute submitted; awaiting Vercel Support resolution."
